# DillClaw Resolver — Environment Variables
# Copy this file to .env and edit as needed.
# These can also be exported in your shell or set in your launchd/systemd config.

# ── HTTP server ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Port the resolver listens on (default: 9474)
# DILLCLAW_PORT=9474

# ── Registry source ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# When DILLCLAW_REGISTRY_BASE_URL is set, the resolver integrates with a
# running Registry server. On startup and at every refresh interval, it
# fetches <base>/list to warm its in-memory snapshot. On a cache miss for
# an exact name, it falls back to <base>/lookup/<name>. Stale-while-
# revalidate is enforced per Resolver Spec §7.3: if /list refresh fails,
# the snapshot is served as stale for up to DILLCLAW_STALE_WINDOW_MS
# (default 900s, max 1800s), after which /resolve returns REGISTRY_UNAVAILABLE.
#
# When unset, the local registry.json file is used. Local mode re-reads the
# file on every resolution, so edits are picked up without a restart.
#
# Example (Registry running on default port 9475):
# DILLCLAW_REGISTRY_BASE_URL=http://localhost:9475

# Legacy variable, accepted as an alias for DILLCLAW_REGISTRY_BASE_URL for
# backward compatibility. Set this to the same value (the base URL) — not
# to a /list or /capabilities path. If both are set, DILLCLAW_REGISTRY_BASE_URL
# takes precedence.
# DILLCLAW_REGISTRY_URL=http://localhost:9475

# How often to refresh the remote registry, in milliseconds (default: 60000 = 60s)
# Ignored in local mode.
# DILLCLAW_REGISTRY_REFRESH_MS=60000

# Stale-while-revalidate window in milliseconds (default: 900000 = 15min).
# Clamped to the spec maximum of 1800000 (30min).
# DILLCLAW_STALE_WINDOW_MS=900000

# ── DNSO signature verification ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Path to the DNSO Ed25519 public key in PEM format. The resolver verifies
# DNSO signatures on every Capability Record using the Registry v0.1.4 /
# v0.2.7 signing profile (canonical JSON over ten top-level signed fields,
# base64url-encoded Ed25519 signatures).
#
# If the key is configured, signed records that fail verification are
# REJECTED (not just scored down). Records with missing signatures are
# only returned when the caller includes "allow_unsigned": true in the
# /resolve request body.
#
# Default: <resolver-dir>/dnso_public.pem
#
# To bootstrap with a test key that signs the bundled sample registry:
#     node tools/generate-keys.js
#
# DILLCLAW_DNSO_PUBLIC_KEY=/path/to/dnso_public.pem

# ── Diagnostic mode ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# When DILLCLAW_DIAGNOSTIC_MODE=1, signature eligibility checks are relaxed:
# invalid signatures are scored but not rejected, and missing signatures
# are returned without requiring caller opt-in. Intended for development
# and debugging only. NEVER enable in production.
# DILLCLAW_DIAGNOSTIC_MODE=0
